Q: Elasticsearch re-index
A: <p>There is no magic here , you will need to maintain some kind of timestamp field which is updated whenever a insertion or change happens to the row. Also make sure the primary key is made as the document ID , that way updated documents are over written and not created as duplicates.</p>

<p>I would recommend <a href="https://github.com/jprante/elasticsearch-jdbc" rel="nofollow">this JDBC importer</a> written by 
Jörg Prante.</p>

<p>In README , he has explained the incremental usage using the following - </p>

<pre><code>{
    "type" : "jdbc",
    "jdbc" : {
        "url" : "jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/test",
        "user" : "",
        "password" : "",
        "sql" : [
            {
                "statement" : "select * from \"products\" where \"mytimestamp\" &gt; ?",
                "parameter" : [ "$metrics.lastexecutionstart" ]
            }
        ],
        "index" : "my_jdbc_index",
        "type" : "my_jdbc_type"
    }
